{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Library repos never track builder-generated files: <crate>/src/api.rs is regenerated by every rebuild to mirror the libraries on THIS box, and <crate>/Cargo.lock resolves THIS box's dependency tree - shipping either dirties every other instance's checkout after its first build. Makes a repo conform, as mechanism: git rm --cached every tracked Cargo.lock and src/api.rs (files stay on disk), appends an anchored ignore line for each crate's pair (a crate = a directory holding a tracked Cargo.toml, the root included) that git does not already ignore (check-ignore), commits with `message` (empty = a standard message), pushes when the branch tracks a remote. Idempotent: a conforming repo answers ok with committed:false. Refuses role canon (its workspace Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose), master/main (branches always - start_branch or carry_branch first), a merge in flight, and a non-empty index (pre-staged work would ride into the commit). Returns {status, msg, branch, untracked:[paths], ignored:[lines], committed, pushed, push_err, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"message","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"slhoyo1a0740a96d8s3","readers":[],"time":1788653269716,"username":"system","writers":[]}